.TH TAEMA.UNIT 5 "2026-10-30" "taema 0.8.0" "Tæma Manual"
.SH NAME
taema.unit \- tæma unit file format
.SH DESCRIPTION
Units match apps and scopes and say how to stop them. Files live in
.IR /etc/taema/units
(system) and
.IR ~/.config/taema/units
(user); later directories win unless a user tombstone masks the name
.RB ( taema\ unit\ disable ).
Lint with
.BR "taema unit lint" ,
dry-run matches with
.BR "taema unit dry-run" ,
test the ladder with
.BR "taema unit test" .
.SH UNIT
.TP
.B [unit] name
Unit name. App units match processes; scope units match explicit scopes.
.TP
.B [unit] kind
\fBapp\fR or \fBscope\fR.
.TP
.B [unit] stop_when_unneeded
Stop the scope when nothing uses it (GC). Detached servers that should
survive logout combine this with
.B [kill] survive_logout.
.TP
.B [unit] group_by_qmp, group_by_env
Optional grouping keys for VM-backed apps.
.SH MATCH
.TP
.B [match] exe, comm, cmdline_contains
How to recognize the app. App units need at least one. Prefer \fBexe\fR;
a bare \fBcomm\fR that matches every process of that name is rejected as
over-broad unless \fBcmdline_contains\fR narrows it.
.TP
.B [match] env_exclude
Table of environment values that disqualify a match.
.SH KILL
.TP
.B [kill] graceful
Seconds to wait after SIGTERM before SIGKILL. Default follows the daemon.
.TP
.B [kill] keep
List of exe basenames moved to shared/ instead of killed, even without a
detected edge (for example shared adb servers).
.TP
.B [kill] hook
Path to an executable stop hook.
.TP
.B [kill] never_stop, survive_logout
Never stop this unit; survive logout (requires \fBstop_when_unneeded\fR).
.SH GC
.TP
.B [gc] keep_while_children
Keep the scope while it has children (for tmux-like servers).
.SH MEM
.TP
.B [mem] class, background
Memory class (\fBapp\fR, \fBvm\fR) and whether the workload is background
work for reclaim priority.
.SH WINDOW
.TP
.B [window] backend, requires_window
Compositor backend and whether the app needs a window to stay alive.
.TP
.B [desktop] app_id, on_last_window
Desktop identity and what happens on the last window close:
\fBask\fR, \fBquit\fR, or \fBkeep\fR.
.SH CHILDREN
.TP
.B [[children]] name, ancestor_comm|comm, binds_to
Carve sub-scopes out of an adopted tree. Each child binds to its own root
process: when that process exits, the child scope stops. Names become
\fIname\fR-\fIpid\fR leaves (for example \fBsession-4242\fR).
.SH SOURCE
.TP
.B [source] learned
True when the learner wrote the file. Masks and packs never touch it.
.SH EXAMPLE
.PP
.nf
[unit]
name = "app-herdr"
kind = "app"
stop_when_unneeded = true

[match]
comm = "herdr"
cmdline_contains = "server"

[kill]
survive_logout = true
graceful = 10

[gc]
keep_while_children = true
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR taema (1),
.BR taema.toml (5),
.BR taema-learning (7)
